{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the actual retained receipt for the fixed harness (CheckRun 238d3a23d8624c438b85ec18f90a7b2b: completed, tests_passed, exit 0, 10 parsed CA_EVENT observations, 0 parse errors) and closed out both registered questions as source-and-evidence explained with no defect asserted. Campaign admission (events 0-5): the node is promotable yet has_unapplied=true with applied=1/committed=2 and entry2_type=EntryConfChangeV2, and both MsgHup and the term-carrying MsgTimeoutNow leave it StateFollower(term 1) with 0 messages - the runner log shows the same suppression reason on both paths - while after raftLog.appliedTo(2,0) it becomes candidate at term 2 with MsgVote to voters [2,3], and the control with an identical applied/committed gap but a normal entry at index 2 campaigns immediately, so the suppression is keyed on the entry type and is transient rather than a stale-voter-set campaign. ReadIndex across a term change (events 6-9): the admitted request (unconfirmed_reads=1, admission commit=2) is dropped after the term change (read_states=0, ctx_A_completed=false, confirmed/ unconfirmed=0) rather than answered stale, the confirmation path still works on the new leader (ctx_B_completed=true with index_B=3 equal to the commit index at admission), and that lossiness is the caller duty the Node.ReadIndex contract already states. Both necessary gaps are answered resolved, two observed behaviors are promoted as execution-backed knowledge citing the exact receipt indices, and each interpretation carries its counterevidence and limits (direct Step of MsgReadIndex rather than the Node API, one term-change trigger, supplied Config.Applied for the store-level probe). I also extended the harness with a third case for the one boundary the two answers leave open - whether a leadership transfer requested for a transferee whose committed conf change is unapplied is a bounded cost or a lost duty - and requested a fresh isolated execution of that extended harness (probes A/B unchanged, probe C added; no previous_id because this investigation has no predecessor experiment). Draft-side that probe showed leadTransferee set while the transferee stays follower, ErrProposalDropped during the window, leadTransferee cleared after one electionTimeout with the leader still leader and proposals accepted again, and the retry completing once the transferee's applied index caught up, but those operands are construction feedback only and await the receipt.\"}"}}
